# Press the swap-weapons command ('-') on a character with NO default melee or
# ranged weapon set. Character::Exchange (src/Inv.cpp) takes its first early
# path: it prints the explanatory "You need to set your default melee and
# ranged weapons ..." line and then, before inc-3ax, also printed the false
# "You fumble the items you were trying to exchange, dropping them!" line.
#
# WHY A FIXTURE. tools/fixtures/chars/lizardfolk-monk-seed1.sav carries no
# default weapons, so the swap command cannot even begin; that is the path under
# test. The character is frozen, so the same save takes the same path on every
# run.
#
# WHY THE ESC. While the inventory manager owns the screen the queued messages
# are not drawn, so the after-dash dump shows only the explanatory line. The
# ESC leaves the inventory and lets Game::Play dump the queue onto the message
# window, which is where the false fumble line shows up. tools/check_exchange_no_false_fumble.sh
# reads both dumps.
#
# Run with a fixed seed; the check supplies one.

@dump:arrival

-               # swap weapons: Character::Exchange, early path (no defaults)
@dump:after-dash

ESC             # leave the inventory; the queued messages are drawn now
@dump:after-esc

# One real turn, so the run counts as a session (headless.sh reports NO
# GAMEPLAY otherwise). The messages above are already dumped.
s
@dump:after-turn
